# Editors and tools that save atomically drop a temporary sibling next to the
# real file (pdp-specifications.liquid.tmp.24812.e7f129d0f225, foo.liquid~,
# .foo.liquid.swp). The `theme dev` watcher picks those up mid-write and the
# upload fails with "Must have a .liquid file extension", which then wedges the
# whole sync until the server is restarted. Ignoring them keeps the watcher on
# real files only.
#
# The temp patterns are deliberately spelled out per real extension rather than
# using a loose `*.tmp.*`: assets/jquery.tmpl.min.js is a required file, and a
# broad pattern anywhere near it is not worth the risk. Both the bare and `**/`
# forms are listed because a leading glob does not always cross a separator.

*.tmp
**/*.tmp

*.liquid.tmp.*
**/*.liquid.tmp.*
*.json.tmp.*
**/*.json.tmp.*
*.css.tmp.*
**/*.css.tmp.*
*.js.tmp.*
**/*.js.tmp.*

# Editor backups and swap files
*~
**/*~
*.swp
**/*.swp
*.swo
**/*.swo
*.orig
**/*.orig
*.rej
**/*.rej
*.bak
**/*.bak

# OS noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/Thumbs.db
.validate-theme-settings.js
